# Pipeline trigger

When the user attaches `@pipeline <brief>`, run the full-stack agent pack end to end for that feature. Parse the brief for a `slug=<slug>`; default to a kebab-case of the brief.

## Setup
```
node scripts/capture.mjs --check
mkdir -p .agent/<slug>/spec
```

## Sequence (do not collapse; each role hands off only its written artifact)
1. **context-loader** (glm-5.2): `node scripts/introspect-db.mjs --out .agent/<slug>/schema.sql`; if a design URL is in the brief, `node scripts/capture.mjs --url <url> --out .agent/<slug> --label target`. Write `.agent/<slug>/context.md`.
2. **planner** (swe-1.7, VISION): write `spec/data-model.md`, `spec/contract.md`, `spec/plan.md`, `spec/visual-spec.md` (if UI in scope) per `.cursor/agents/planner.md`.
3. **plan-verifier** (swe-1.7, VISION) [GATE]: audit, write `audit-1.md`. Below 0.90 or any data-model gap -> back to planner. No code, no migration until APPROVED. Max 3 rounds.
4. **db-migrator** (glm-5.2): if data-model changed, edit schema, generate, read SQL, apply to scratch DB, re-introspect. Expand/contract for destructive.
5. **implementer** (glm-5.2, NO VISION): close the screenshot. Build contract package -> db queries -> Hono handlers (authz first) -> Next.js UI (every named state) -> tests against Testcontainers Postgres. Never mock the DB.
6. **behavior-reviewer** (glm-5.2): typecheck/lint/vitest/playwright real output, OpenAPI diff, authz on every touched endpoint, EXPLAIN ANALYZE every new query. Write `review-iter-<N>.md`.
7. **visual-reviewer** (swe-1.7, VISION, if UI in scope): `capture.mjs` the build, `diff.mjs` against target, write property deltas ranked by impact.

## Routing on failure
- implementation bug -> implementer
- schema defect -> db-migrator
- spec defect (code matches spec but not the target) -> planner -> plan-verifier -> implementer
Max 3 rounds. Report final scores and residual deltas. Stop and ask the operator if a gate fails 3 times.

## Constraints
- Scraped logos, fonts, photography are reference only. Substitute project assets before shipping. Respect robots.txt and terms of service.
- The implementer must never read a `.png`. If it reaches for the design, the spec has a hole -> back to planner.
